index 5c60a134..17753969 100644
--- a/docs/Reference/Reply.md
+++ b/docs/Reference/Reply.md
@@ -728,6 +728,15 @@ fastify.get('/streams', async function (request, reply) {
 })
 ```
 
+Streams are piped to the response as they are, so the chunks they emit are
+written unchanged. Over HTTP/2, handing a very large chunk to a single write
+can stall the whole session if the client cancels the request while that data
+is still queued, affecting the other requests multiplexed on the same
+connection. When a stream is under your control, emit data in reasonably sized
+chunks (for example, the default 64 KiB `highWaterMark` of
+`fs.createReadStream`) instead of a few very large ones. Buffer and string
+payloads are chunked by Fastify itself.
+
 #### Buffers
 <a id="send-buffers"></a>
 
